<%# Live response tally, replaced over Action Cable as answers land.

    `live` is false on the page's own first render and true on every broadcast,
    which is what distinguishes "here are the numbers" from "these just changed" —
    the second gets the pulse and the refresh affordance, because the charts below
    are still showing the older aggregation until the creator asks for a rebuild.
    Rebuilding them automatically would re-aggregate every response for every
    viewer on every submission, and move the page under someone reading it.

    Two pills, over the empty half of the map rather than in the header: the
    headline number is what the page is about, and the header is where the
    controls live. Completion is a RATE here, not the raw count it used to be —
    "339" beside "465" is a subtraction the reader has to do, and the answer
    (73%) is the thing they wanted. The count is still in the title.

    The "asked to hear" count that used to sit beside these is gone; it was a
    third number competing with the two that describe the results themselves. %>
<div id="results-live" class="rmap-tally">
  <div class="rmap-pill rmap-pill--count">
    <span class="rh-count-num<%= " is-pulsing" if live %>"><%= responders %></span>
    <span class="rh-count-word">response<%= responders == 1 ? "" : "s" %></span>
  </div>

  <%# No rate before there is anything to rate: 0% of nobody is not a fact
      about the Verto, it is a fact about it not having started. %>
  <% if responders.positive? %>
    <div class="rmap-pill rmap-pill--rate"
         title="<%= completed %> of <%= responders %> reached the end">
      <span class="rmap-rate-num"><%= (completed * 100.0 / responders).round %>%</span>
      <span class="rmap-rate-word">completed</span>
    </div>
  <% end %>

  <% if live %>
    <%# Reloads just the results frame, so the breakdown rebuilds on demand
        rather than on every incoming answer. %>
    <%= link_to "↻ Refresh breakdown",
          survey_results_path(survey, segment: params[:segment]),
          data: { turbo_frame: "results-feed" },
          class: "rh-refresh" %>
  <% end %>
</div>
